couple months, or a couple weeks in.

00:09:12.927 --> 00:09:15.846
And so, leaving everybody

00:09:15.846 --> 00:09:17.390
you've ever known. Like, this is the first

00:09:17.390 --> 00:09:19.684
time I haven't been around anybody.

00:09:19.684 --> 00:09:20.309
There's nobody in the

00:09:20.309 --> 00:09:21.936
whole state that I know.

00:09:22.687 --> 00:09:23.938
So I'm kinda just going into the

00:09:23.938 --> 00:09:25.398
situation just hoping for the best.

00:09:26.107 --> 00:09:28.359
And mind you, this is what’s so crazy.

00:09:28.359 --> 00:09:29.360
A lot of people probably wouldn't

00:09:29.360 --> 00:09:30.570
believe this. Coach Boyle had

00:09:30.570 --> 00:09:32.863
never even seen me play basketball

00:09:32.863 --> 00:09:34.865
in person before I got there.

00:09:35.491 --> 00:09:36.909
So I'm just going off the fact that the

00:09:36.909 --> 00:09:38.286
assistant coach, Coach Rae, he's

00:09:38.286 --> 00:09:40.246
seen me. And I'm going off the fact,

00:09:40.246 --> 00:09:41.163
like, I think I'm nice.

00:09:41.163 --> 00:09:42.290
So, you're gonna have to, you know

00:09:42.290 --> 00:09:43.082
what I'm saying? You gonna have to

00:09:43.082 --> 00:09:46.127
respect that either way.
- Yeah.
- So, I'm goin’ in,

00:09:46.127 --> 00:09:46.752
you know what I'm saying?

00:09:47.753 --> 00:09:49.797
And then back home, things just

00:09:49.797 --> 00:09:51.674
started to, it felt like, crumble.

00:09:51.674 --> 00:09:53.634
Like, whenever you're not around and

00:09:53.634 --> 00:09:55.261
you're not there to see things happen

00:09:55.261 --> 00:09:56.804
and you're just hearing it from afar,

00:09:57.388 --> 00:09:59.056
it feels like everything's going bad.

00:09:59.056 --> 00:10:01.225
I started having, you know what I'm saying,

00:10:01.225 --> 00:10:02.935
deaths in the family and stuff, like—

00:10:02.935 --> 00:10:04.228
and everything's hitting

00:10:04.228 --> 00:10:06.147
me way harder whenever I'm, you

00:10:06.147 --> 00:10:07.523
know, miles away from my fam.

00:10:07.523 --> 00:10:09.275
So, it was tough for sure.

00:10:09.275 --> 00:10:09.567
But

00:10:10.443 --> 00:10:11.319
it’s crazy.

00:10:11.319 --> 00:10:12.695
Like, I wanted to go home

00:10:12.695 --> 00:10:13.779
so bad. I’m steady calling

00:10:13.779 --> 00:10:14.697
my mom. I was like, “Mom,

00:10:14.697 --> 00:10:15.781
just let me come home.

00:10:15.781 --> 00:10:16.198
Please.”

00:10:16.198 --> 00:10:18.034
Just, like, I'm begging her to

00:10:18.034 --> 00:10:19.702
let me slide back to the crib.
- Yeah.

00:10:19.952 --> 00:10:21.621
But it's crazy how much it helped

00:10:21.621 --> 00:10:23.331
me, and I'm glad I did it for sure.

00:10:23.998 --> 00:10:24.915
And going into college

00:10:24.915 --> 00:10:25.708
was so much easier.

00:10:25.708 --> 00:10:26.709
cuz I was already used to

00:10:26.709 --> 00:10:29.754
being on my own and trying

00:10:29.754 --> 00:10:30.713
to make things happen for myself..

00:10:30.713 --> 00:10:32.381
Clearly, like, Arlington and

00:10:32.381 --> 00:10:33.758
your hometown meant a lot to you.

00:10:33.758 --> 00:10:36.010
So, like, what—how did it also shape

00:10:36.010 --> 00:10:38.929
you as just who you are as Cade?

00:10:38.929 --> 00:10:40.264
- That's where everybody's

00:10:40.264 --> 00:10:42.308
at. And what's crazy,

00:10:42.308 --> 00:10:44.268
It's not even as much about

00:10:44.268 --> 00:10:47.813
you know, visiting home. But it's

00:10:47.813 --> 00:10:49.732
missing home and then trying to

00:10:50.107 --> 00:10:52.276
still get in the gym every day

00:10:52.276 --> 00:10:53.903
and put your work in and still

00:10:54.445 --> 00:10:55.988
be first in every sprint and

00:10:55.988 --> 00:10:57.031
still—you know what I'm saying?

00:10:57.448 --> 00:10:58.324
Like, that's the

00:10:58.324 --> 00:10:59.909
part that's tough for guys.

00:10:59.909 --> 00:11:01.285
Whenever they get out to Montverde or

00:11:01.285 --> 00:11:03.329
whatever, you know, that separation

00:11:03.329 --> 00:11:05.414
gets tough and then, whenever things get hard

00:11:05.414 --> 00:11:07.208
for you and you see some adversity,

00:11:07.792 --> 00:11:08.959
you know, you start missing home.

00:11:08.959 --> 00:11:10.294
That's whenever you usually get to

00:11:10.753 --> 00:11:13.005
be at the crib and take some time

00:11:13.005 --> 00:11:14.840
off, but you know, you're gone.

00:11:14.840 --> 00:11:16.217
You're at Montverde. Just, you can't—

00:11:16.217 --> 00:11:16.926
you don't really have it.

00:11:16.926 --> 00:11:17.218
So,

00:11:17.968 --> 00:11:19.970
you know, I didn't realize how much

00:11:19.970 --> 00:11:21.764
I needed Arlington until I left.

00:11:21.764 --> 00:11:24.475
And then I'm like—
- That’s when you know.
- It meant everything to me.

00:11:24.475 --> 00:11:26.352
So, yeah, it saved me, man.

00:11:26.352 --> 00:11:27.353
It made me who I am today.

00:11:27.353 --> 00:11:29.355
I'm born and raised over there.

00:11:29.355 --> 00:11:30.398
So, yeah.

00:11:30.439 --> 00:11:31.732
- Yeah.
- That’s home for sure.

00:11:31.732 --> 00:11:33.859
- So, what I wanna know is your

00:11:33.859 --> 00:11:36.612
mentality with picking the

00:11:36.612 --> 00:11:38.989
spots and taking over games.

00:11:38.989 --> 00:11:40.533
What is Cade’s mentality with

00:11:41.033 --> 00:11:43.452
taking over games?
- For me, every game I'm

00:11:43.452 --> 00:11:44.704
trying to eat, you know what I'm saying?

00:11:44.704 --> 00:11:46.539
Like, obviously I'm going into every

00:11:46.539 --> 00:11:50.042
game wanting 50 or whatever, but

00:11:50.042 --> 00:11:52.837
obviously game plans, things like that,

00:11:53.254 --> 00:11:54.964
it's not as easy as that.

00:11:54.964 --> 00:11:57.091
So, I know I'mma leave my mark

00:11:57.091 --> 00:12:00.094
on every game and, like, that—I

00:12:00.094 --> 00:12:01.470
go into every game knowing that's a

00:12:01.470 --> 00:12:03.097
given. Like, I'm gonna do something,

00:12:03.097 --> 00:12:03.931
you know what I'm saying?

00:12:03.931 --> 00:12:05.891
Other teams gonna know why

00:12:05.891 --> 00:12:07.226
they say what they say about me.

00:12:08.352 --> 00:12:10.104
And every game, it just

00:12:10.104 --> 00:12:12.064
felt like the first half would

00:12:12.064 --> 00:12:13.983
slip away from it a little bit.

00:12:14.483 --> 00:12:15.317
Like, I'm tryna make

00:12:15.317 --> 00:12:16.569
things happen, whatever.

00:12:16.902 --> 00:12:18.279
And the first half would slip, and

00:12:18.279 --> 00:12:19.989
I'm like, “Oh, I gotta do some work

00:12:19.989 --> 00:12:22.032
in the second.” Every time. And there

00:12:22.032 --> 00:12:23.576
was some games where, you know, things

00:12:23.576 --> 00:12:25.870
were going easy for me in the first

00:12:25.870 --> 00:12:28.122
half or whatever, but yeah, it was—

00:12:28.497 --> 00:12:29.790
- Yeah.
- I wish I woulda turnt

00:12:29.790 --> 00:12:30.499
up a little bit more.

00:12:30.499 --> 00:12:31.792
And then the narrative

00:12:31.792 --> 00:12:33.919
started going, whatever. You know, “He

00:12:33.919 --> 00:12:36.130
only turn up for the second half.
So, you know

00:12:36.130 --> 00:12:39.800
how it go, but—
- How did that approach,

00:12:39.800 --> 00:12:42.303
like, get so instilled in you with,

00:12:42.303 --> 00:12:43.721
like, doing what it takes to win?

00:12:43.721 --> 00:12:44.555
Cuz it's hard.

00:12:44.555 --> 00:12:45.598
Because sometimes, like you

00:12:45.598 --> 00:12:47.183
said, you might be off, but you

00:12:47.183 --> 00:12:48.559
know when to take over the game.

00:12:48.559 --> 00:12:49.769
Sometimes you might be flowing.

00:12:49.769 --> 00:12:51.020
You gotta know when to pick your spots

00:12:51.020 --> 00:12:52.605
and everything. But to win the ballgame,

00:12:52.605 --> 00:12:54.190
you have to do a lot of things to win.

00:12:54.190 --> 00:12:55.775
So, like, how did you get to that point?

00:12:56.484 --> 00:12:59.403
- I've think the big, I think the main

00:12:59.403 --> 00:13:01.822
beginning for me was the Texas Titans.

00:13:01.822 --> 00:13:03.199
I started playing

00:13:03.199 --> 00:13:04.241
with them in fourth grade.

00:13:04.283 --> 00:13:08.370
So, like, you know what I’m saying?
We’re young when

00:13:08.370 --> 00:13:10.623
we started this, and then we’re winning

00:13:10.623 --> 00:13:12.750
games, and we were tough.

00:13:12.750 --> 00:13:15.377
Like, we're—nationals, we're doing all

00:13:15.377 --> 00:13:16.504
this stuff that, you know what I'm saying,

00:13:16.504 --> 00:13:18.255
these young teams are doing or whatever.

00:13:18.798 --> 00:13:20.299
And, you know, I think the biggest

00:13:20.299 --> 00:13:21.967
thing for us was our togetherness.

00:13:21.967 --> 00:13:24.553
Like, everybody knew the Titans,

00:13:24.553 --> 00:13:25.971
their chemistry was on point.

00:13:26.430 --> 00:13:27.223
No matter what, they're

00:13:27.223 --> 00:13:28.015
gonna make plays for each other.

00:13:28.015 --> 00:13:29.141
Like, they're

00:13:29.141 --> 00:13:30.309
gonna get good shots.

00:13:30.309 --> 00:13:31.727
Maybe they might not hit ‘em,

00:13:31.727 --> 00:13:32.561
but they gonna make sure

00:13:32.561 --> 00:13:34.271
they give each other good shots.
- Yeah.

00:13:34.271 --> 00:13:36.190
And so, playing in a system like that

00:13:36.190 --> 00:13:38.734
since I was a young’un and then growing

00:13:38.734 --> 00:13:40.110
up into that, and then I started

00:13:40.110 --> 00:13:41.445
getting better and better and better.

00:13:42.196 --> 00:13:43.364
Like, I was still used to

00:13:43.364 --> 00:13:44.740
playing that type of basketball.

00:13:44.740 --> 00:13:47.660
So, eventually it just carried

00:13:47.660 --> 00:13:50.412
over.
- I guess it leads into you

00:13:50.412 --> 00:13:51.997
with your leadership as well, because

00:13:51.997 --> 00:13:53.207
they also say that about you everywhere

00:13:53.207 --> 00:13:54.625
you've been, whether it’s Montverde

00:13:54.625 --> 00:13:56.877
or even, you know, Oklahoma State,

00:13:56.877 --> 00:13:58.546
and even some of your AAU teammates.

00:13:58.546 --> 00:14:00.464
It's always about, like, “He always

00:14:00.464 --> 00:14:03.592
has a control over the game,” and

00:14:03.592 --> 00:14:04.760
like, and they listen to you,

00:14:04.760 --> 00:14:05.094
right?

00:14:05.135 --> 00:14:06.303
So when you speak, a lot of your

00:14:06.303 --> 00:14:07.596
teammates will make sure they trust you.

00:14:07.596 --> 00:14:08.639
So, you think that also has

00:14:08.639 --> 00:14:09.765
something to do with that?

00:14:09.765 --> 00:14:10.558
With, like, how comfortable

00:14:10.558 --> 00:14:11.350
you are with leadership?

00:14:12.309 --> 00:14:13.227
- Yeah, definitely.

00:14:13.227 --> 00:14:13.644
Definitely.

00:14:13.644 --> 00:14:16.605
And I think that mainly helps

00:14:16.605 --> 00:14:18.190
me with, like, whenever I'm new to

00:14:18.190 --> 00:14:20.150
a room, I don't ever feel

00:14:20.150 --> 00:14:22.361
like, you know, a room sways me into,

00:14:22.945 --> 00:14:25.281
you know, going with the majority.

00:14:25.281 --> 00:14:26.448
I feel like that's, that's the

00:14:26.448 --> 00:14:28.325
main thing that my parents have,

00:14:28.325 --> 00:14:29.952
you know, really instilled in me.

00:14:29.952 --> 00:14:32.371
And then after a while, whenever my name

00:14:32.371 --> 00:14:34.164
started to blow up and things like that,

00:14:34.874 --> 00:14:36.792
I think the most important thing was

00:14:36.792 --> 00:14:38.627
just not trying to force things on ‘em.

00:14:39.169 --> 00:14:41.255
Like, I feel like a lot of times, you know,

00:14:41.255 --> 00:14:42.882
somebody might be the most known or

00:14:42.882 --> 00:14:44.300
the best player, and they try to force

00:14:44.300 --> 00:14:46.427
leadership on guys and stuff like that.

00:14:46.427 --> 00:14:47.928
And it's not—like, a lot of times,

00:14:47.928 --> 00:14:49.430
dudes are like, “Bro, you just doin’

00:14:49.430 --> 00:14:51.056
too much,” you know what I'm saying?

00:14:51.056 --> 00:14:53.350
Maybe boost your head up or whatever.

00:14:53.350 --> 00:14:55.978
So, I'm just trying to be natural.

00:14:55.978 --> 00:14:57.563
I try to be me wherever I'm at.

00:14:58.397 --> 00:15:00.733
And, you know, I know I can hoop.

00:15:00.733 --> 00:15:02.943
So, in practice, you have to see me anyways,

00:15:02.943 --> 00:15:03.569
so.

00:15:03.903 --> 00:15:05.112
And I think that as time goes

00:15:05.112 --> 00:15:06.864
on, people just, you know, naturally

00:15:06.864 --> 00:15:08.115
start to gravitate towards me.

00:15:08.282 --> 00:15:09.992
And, you know, I try to do

00:15:09.992 --> 00:15:10.910
what's best for the squad.

00:15:10.910 --> 00:15:13.829
I got my faults too, but I think that's

00:15:13.829 --> 00:15:15.664
why not, you know, trying to force

00:15:15.664 --> 00:15:17.541
leadership helps because whenever I

00:15:17.541 --> 00:15:18.834
make a mistake, you're not gonna

00:15:18.834 --> 00:15:21.295
wanna bash me for it. You gonna wanna

00:15:21.295 --> 00:15:22.671
help me just like I wanna help you.

00:15:22.671 --> 00:15:24.548
So, I think that's probably the main thing.

00:15:24.548 --> 00:15:25.257
I think that's why my

00:15:25.257 --> 00:15:26.717
teams have been pretty good.
- That’s awesome.

00:15:27.217 --> 00:15:28.218
Did some of that have to do

00:15:28.218 --> 00:15:30.429
with just the 2020 class in

00:15:30.429 --> 00:15:33.599
itself? Like, because of how

00:15:33.599 --> 00:15:36.435
talented that, you know—

00:15:37.144 --> 00:15:38.228
at least we view it and I view

00:15:38.228 --> 00:15:39.855
it—as deep as it goes,

00:15:40.064 --> 00:15:41.065
do you think some of that also had to do

00:15:41.065 --> 00:15:42.524
with your class you were in as well?

00:15:43.192 --> 00:15:43.609
- Definitely.

00:15:43.776 --> 00:15:45.694
I think we—I'm so glad

00:15:45.694 --> 00:15:47.613
that I’m in the 2020 class,

00:15:47.613 --> 00:15:48.948
just because of the way that we pushed

00:15:48.948 --> 00:15:52.576
each other. Like, in camps, you

00:15:52.576 --> 00:15:54.161
know, everything. We just, we pushed

00:15:54.161 --> 00:15:55.454
each other to a different level that—

00:15:56.080 --> 00:15:57.456
like, we were friendly with each other.

00:15:57.456 --> 00:16:00.584
We had fun, but I think you

00:16:00.584 --> 00:16:02.878
can ask anybody that ran camps

00:16:03.420 --> 00:16:05.005
with us or anything.

00:16:05.005 --> 00:16:06.966
We never, we never—you know, say if

00:16:06.966 --> 00:16:08.968
we were scrimmaging or whatever,

00:16:08.968 --> 00:16:10.678
we never played friendly.

00:16:10.678 --> 00:16:11.887
Like, we were always pushing each

00:16:11.887 --> 00:16:12.972
other, we were always competing.

00:16:13.597 --> 00:16:14.765
And I think that's

00:16:14.765 --> 00:16:17.309
why we've, in the 2020 class,

00:16:17.309 --> 00:16:18.811
we all went to college and we performed

00:16:18.811 --> 00:16:20.396
well, you know what I'm saying?

00:16:20.396 --> 00:16:22.439
People are starting to see what we do at

00:16:22.439 --> 00:16:24.650
the next level, just because, like, we've

00:16:24.650 --> 00:16:26.986
been competing hard for a long time.

00:16:26.986 --> 00:16:29.029
So, it's carried over. Like, those things

00:16:29.029 --> 00:16:31.657
don't happen by accident.
- The aspirations

00:16:32.324 --> 00:16:34.118
along this whole journey, right?

00:16:34.118 --> 00:16:36.537
You've had ‘em, but now being this

00:16:36.537 --> 00:16:39.123
close to, like, what is the NBA player

00:16:39.123 --> 00:16:42.918
that you're hoping to become?
- The best.

00:16:42.918 --> 00:16:46.005
I'm tryna be that dude. I wanna

00:16:46.005 --> 00:16:48.924
be the best point guard—if they

00:16:48.924 --> 00:16:50.259
list me as a point guard—of all

00:16:50.259 --> 00:16:52.052
time. The best whatever you wanna call it.

00:16:52.928 --> 00:16:55.597
Yeah, I wanna be him. Like,

00:16:55.597 --> 00:16:57.599
I want, whenever dudes think of

00:16:58.350 --> 00:17:01.478
NBA, they think Cunningham is, yeah, one

00:17:01.478 --> 00:17:04.481
of the ones. And, yeah, I'm excited for it.

00:17:05.149 --> 00:17:06.483
I think the biggest thing is, like, you

00:17:06.483 --> 00:17:08.610
know, I've already went through the

00:17:08.610 --> 00:17:09.820
high school thing, college thing.

00:17:09.820 --> 00:17:11.321
That's like the, you know, the amateur,

00:17:12.448 --> 00:17:13.741
you know, amateur basketball or whatever.

00:17:13.741 --> 00:17:16.827
And being able to see myself next

00:17:16.827 --> 00:17:18.328
to No. 1 ranked or, you know

00:17:18.328 --> 00:17:19.580
what I'm saying, whatever, was cool.

00:17:19.580 --> 00:17:20.372
But now that, you

00:17:20.789 --> 00:17:22.583
know what I'm saying, I really get to

00:17:22.583 --> 00:17:25.002
